          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Summary: Observation of the movement in the sky of a first light followed by a second on the same trajectory and at constant speed and distance: rare observation of the passage of the ISS and the Japanese space cargo HTV.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "55c7abe0173746041172f8200cb13977f1eefd4e8573a6b66e383cfd7bf85b3c"
        },
        {
          "end_ms": null,
          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-9f49d16516f00f449d8adbd0",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-9c35acaf51fdbc7f807eeb79",
          "segment_index": 12,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-9c35acaf51fdbc7f807eeb79",
          "source_text_sha256": "432afe803bfed298794c84ac8d2bbf59bf8ef9c26810a78e041016ec683c1638",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 27, 2012, between 4:20 and 4:25 AM, a witness was intrigued by the silent passage across the sky of a milky white, oval-shaped light. The observation lasted approximately 45 seconds before a second orange-colored light phenomenon appeared, perfectly tracking the trajectory of the first light phenomenon. These lights moved at constant speed and deviation on a straight trajectory. The phenomenon disappeared, hidden by the landscape. The witness had the luck to observe a passage of the International Space Station (ISS) with a magnitude of -3 (like Venus) and the Japanese space cargo HTV with a magnitude of 3, a few hours before its docking with the ISS (see Calsky log and Canadian Space Agency website), on the same orbit, a few degrees apart. This case is classified \"A\" as perfectly identified observation of a very rare ISS + Japanese space cargo HTV passage. Note that the witness described the object as large as the Moon, and for an observation duration of 45 seconds: this type of estimation error is not uncommon for surprising phenomena.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "d9b4ef2bbcdc43e30b61153d45b8de8bf6593513cabd294267bdc677a857a49f"
        }
      ],
